# Git delegation

Applies to **this hub git repo** (the folder that contains `Agents/AGENTS.md` and `.cursor/hooks/`).

- In **this hub repo**, do **not** run `git` or `gh` in the parent agent shell. Delegate to **git-coordinator**. Relay user choices. Trust the **Git Report**.
- **Resume** the same git-coordinator agent id for **Yes** / **No** / **Preview**, add-before-commit **Yes** / **No**, **Custom** / **Agent generated**, and merge-menu ids. Do not spawn a new Task per relay unless the last run aborted.
- Do not open `subagents.md` or `git-coordinator.md`. The Task prompt tells git-coordinator to read `Agents/Subagents/git-coordinator/git-coordinator.md` and `user-config.md` in that folder. If a User Rule lists those paths, do not open them. Put the paths in the Task prompt only.
- On a `git` or `gh` command, read `Agents/Rules/git-delegation/git-delegation.md` for the menus, then stop. Do not open that file on any other prompt.
- In **any other git repo**, the parent **may** run `git`/`gh`. Ask which **repo_path** when the user wants the coordinator on a specific repo.
